WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:15.174
Every parent's worst nightmare:

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.613
July 20, 2012,

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:23.494
my phone rings at 4:30 in the morning.

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:27.111
It's my son Alex's girlfriend, Amanda,

00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:28.621
saying hysterically,

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:33.550
"Tom, Tom, there's been a shooting,

00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:35.809
and they dragged me out of the theater.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:38.241
They wouldn't let me stay.

00:00:38.265 --> 00:00:40.787
I wanted to [stay],
but they dragged me out."

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:44.249
I say to Amanda,

00:00:44.273 --> 00:00:46.611
"Amanda, are you OK? Have you been hurt?"

00:00:47.455 --> 00:00:51.086
And she said no, that she was fine,

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.307
that Alex had saved her life.

00:00:54.536 --> 00:00:55.936
I then say,

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.017
"Amanda, where's Alex?"

00:00:59.781 --> 00:01:02.029
And she says, sobbing,

00:01:02.053 --> 00:01:04.688
"I don't know, we can't find him.

00:01:04.712 --> 00:01:06.400
They dragged me out of the theater.

00:01:06.424 --> 00:01:07.659
They made me leave.

00:01:07.683 --> 00:01:09.112
He was shot.

00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:11.944
I tried to wake him up,
but I couldn't wake him up.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.786
He wouldn't get up.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.285
They dragged me away.
I didn't want to leave him."

00:01:18.856 --> 00:01:22.047
And I say to Amanda,

00:01:24.253 --> 00:01:26.226
"The last time you saw Alex,

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:28.726
was he bleeding?

00:01:29.607 --> 00:01:35.734
Did you have any of his blood on you?"

00:01:36.855 --> 00:01:41.139
And she cries, "Yeah, a lot,"

00:01:41.163 --> 00:01:42.805
and breaks down.

00:01:44.886 --> 00:01:46.438
Alex loved Amanda.

00:01:47.088 --> 00:01:50.243
And he was one of the most
honorable men on earth,

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:52.319
and at the age of 24,

00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:57.135
he had to make the decision
to risk his life

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:59.791
in order to ensure she would live.

00:02:01.298 --> 00:02:04.914
I knew in my heart if he couldn't get up,

00:02:06.486 --> 00:02:07.867
he was dead.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.176
I had just arrived

00:02:13.624 --> 00:02:14.982
the night before

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.059
with my wife Caren

00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:19.974
and my youngest son

00:02:21.704 --> 00:02:24.081
for a week's vacation in Hawaii.

00:02:25.453 --> 00:02:26.871
We were literally

00:02:27.883 --> 00:02:30.595
3,300 miles away.

00:02:32.294 --> 00:02:36.872
Caren and I frantically started
calling his cell phone,

00:02:36.896 --> 00:02:38.060
to no avail.

00:02:38.084 --> 00:02:40.105
We left multiple messages.

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.668
We then turned to the media.

00:02:44.582 --> 00:02:46.388
But all we could find

00:02:47.896 --> 00:02:50.301
was information on the murderer

00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:52.498
and his booby-trapped apartment.

00:02:54.126 --> 00:02:57.861
We tried calling
the Aurora police station,

00:02:57.885 --> 00:03:00.590
but it was impossible to get an answer.

00:03:00.614 --> 00:03:02.968
But in hindsight, it was understandable.

00:03:03.669 --> 00:03:05.271
They were dealing with

00:03:06.355 --> 00:03:09.561
12 dead, 70 injured,

00:03:10.619 --> 00:03:13.249
the carnage so bad,

00:03:13.273 --> 00:03:17.842
the police had to bring
some of the victims to the hospitals

00:03:17.866 --> 00:03:19.734
in the backs of their police cars,

00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:22.596
because they had run out of ambulances.

00:03:24.562 --> 00:03:28.573
It was a horrific and chaotic scene.

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:33.309
We would never see Alex again,

00:03:34.692 --> 00:03:37.266
his injuries so severe

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.004
I had to shield even his mom

00:03:41.028 --> 00:03:43.241
from looking upon him,

00:03:43.265 --> 00:03:48.011
for fear that would be
the lasting image of him in her mind.

00:03:49.392 --> 00:03:52.635
But you know who we would see
again and again?

00:03:52.659 --> 00:03:54.027
The murderer.

00:03:54.476 --> 00:03:57.567
His pictures were everywhere.

00:03:58.796 --> 00:04:02.160
One article was six paragraphs long

00:04:03.674 --> 00:04:08.569
and featured his name 41 times.

00:04:09.427 --> 00:04:12.664
The media had made him famous.

00:04:14.468 --> 00:04:17.962
But my firstborn son, Alex,

00:04:17.986 --> 00:04:19.311
a hero,

00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:23.837
was absent from those initial reports.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:30.468
Caren and I immediately realized
that there was something wrong

00:04:31.431 --> 00:04:35.483
with the way the media responds
to these random mass shootings

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.184
since Columbine.

00:04:37.961 --> 00:04:40.264
We started doing research,

00:04:41.666 --> 00:04:43.636
and we realized

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.492
that if we could change

00:04:46.476 --> 00:04:48.470
the way the media reports,

00:04:48.494 --> 00:04:52.262
we could reduce the amount of shootings

00:04:52.286 --> 00:04:53.642
and save lives.

00:04:55.148 --> 00:05:02.106
(Applause)

00:05:04.074 --> 00:05:05.646
Let me explain.

00:05:07.829 --> 00:05:12.979
Almost every single random mass shooter

00:05:13.003 --> 00:05:14.849
has something in common.

00:05:16.035 --> 00:05:18.228
Can anybody guess what that is?

00:05:20.468 --> 00:05:22.363
They want notoriety.

00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:25.454
They want to be famous.

00:05:25.478 --> 00:05:27.372
In fact,

00:05:27.396 --> 00:05:32.946
these murderers
are telling us this themselves.

00:05:33.684 --> 00:05:35.993
The Sandy Hook murderer

00:05:36.017 --> 00:05:38.235
kept a spreadsheet

00:05:38.259 --> 00:05:43.085
of previous mass murderers
and their number of kills.

00:05:43.982 --> 00:05:48.988
The Orlando Pulse nightclub murderer

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.374
called a local news station --

00:05:53.398 --> 00:05:55.451
during his attack! --

00:05:55.475 --> 00:06:00.244
and then stopped to check Facebook
to see if he'd gone viral.

00:06:01.355 --> 00:06:03.192
The Parkland murderer

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.222
recorded and posted

00:06:07.246 --> 00:06:09.095
a video

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:10.269
stating,

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.906
"When you see me on the news,
you'll know who I am."

00:06:15.981 --> 00:06:20.662
The Aurora theater murderer
told his psychiatrist

00:06:20.686 --> 00:06:26.886
that he recognized he couldn't
make an impact on the world in science,

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.020
but he could become famous

00:06:30.044 --> 00:06:31.845
by blowing people up.

00:06:32.932 --> 00:06:35.143
And most telling,

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:38.584
the Umpqua Community College murderer

00:06:38.608 --> 00:06:43.056
wrote on his blog
about a previous mass murderer,

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.917
saying,

00:06:44.941 --> 00:06:48.747
"I've noticed that people like him

00:06:48.771 --> 00:06:51.652
are all alone and unknown,

00:06:51.676 --> 00:06:54.196
but when they spill a little blood,

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.144
the whole world knows who they are."

00:06:57.881 --> 00:07:03.537
A man who was known by no one
is now known by everyone,

00:07:03.561 --> 00:07:07.642
his face splashed across every screen,

00:07:07.666 --> 00:07:09.452
his name on the lips

00:07:09.476 --> 00:07:11.628
of everyone on the planet,

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.474
all in one day.

00:07:16.277 --> 00:07:18.817
It seems like the more people you kill,

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.972
the more you're in the limelight.

00:07:24.003 --> 00:07:26.426
These are just a few examples.

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:29.411
I could go on and on.

00:07:29.435 --> 00:07:33.937
These murderers are telling us
they want to be famous

00:07:33.961 --> 00:07:36.486
like the murderers before them,

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:43.141
and the media continues to give them
exactly what they seek:

00:07:43.165 --> 00:07:44.948
notoriety.

00:07:47.763 --> 00:07:50.539
The gun debate is very emotional,

00:07:51.579 --> 00:07:56.374
and our mental health issues
are very complicated.

00:07:57.541 --> 00:07:59.609
Both will take time to correct.

00:08:01.308 --> 00:08:04.397
But to reduce the carnage,

00:08:04.421 --> 00:08:07.517
we don't need an act of Congress.

00:08:08.213 --> 00:08:11.219
What we need is an act of conscience

00:08:11.243 --> 00:08:15.119
on the producers
and consumers of mass media

00:08:15.143 --> 00:08:18.240
to remove the reward of notoriety.

00:08:18.771 --> 00:08:24.821
(Applause)

00:08:27.928 --> 00:08:29.605
So to save lives,

00:08:30.613 --> 00:08:32.990
Caren and I launched "No Notoriety,"

00:08:34.171 --> 00:08:36.917
dedicated to challenging the media

00:08:36.941 --> 00:08:39.193
to protect our communities

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:43.105
by adhering to these
research-backed principles.

00:08:43.607 --> 00:08:46.905
One: report all the facts

00:08:46.929 --> 00:08:48.830
on the mindset,

00:08:48.854 --> 00:08:50.192
demographics

00:08:50.216 --> 00:08:54.190
and motivational profile
of these shooters,

00:08:54.214 --> 00:08:58.390
but minimize their names and images,

00:08:58.414 --> 00:08:59.908
unless they're at large.

00:09:00.789 --> 00:09:05.881
Two: limit the use of the shooter's name

00:09:05.905 --> 00:09:07.368
to once per piece,

00:09:07.392 --> 00:09:09.157
never in the headlines

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:12.359
and no pictures in prominent locations.

00:09:12.788 --> 00:09:13.948
And three --

00:09:15.206 --> 00:09:16.362
Three.

00:09:16.386 --> 00:09:17.441
(Laughter)

00:09:17.465 --> 00:09:18.951
I'm not good with numbers.

00:09:18.975 --> 00:09:20.181
(Laughter)

00:09:21.154 --> 00:09:26.831
Refuse to publish
any self-serving material

00:09:26.855 --> 00:09:28.642
provided by the shooters.

00:09:29.326 --> 00:09:34.680
(Applause)

00:09:37.058 --> 00:09:38.813
To be clear:

00:09:38.837 --> 00:09:41.649
this is not an infringement

00:09:41.673 --> 00:09:45.257
on anyone's First Amendment rights.

00:09:45.281 --> 00:09:48.401
This is not censorship.

00:09:48.425 --> 00:09:51.189
We are merely asking the media

00:09:51.213 --> 00:09:56.312
to leverage guidelines
they already have in place.

00:09:56.336 --> 00:09:58.051
For example,

00:09:58.075 --> 00:10:00.622
the media does not report

00:10:00.646 --> 00:10:03.955
on journalists that have been kidnapped

00:10:03.979 --> 00:10:05.954
in order to protect them.

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:09.516
The media does not report

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.472
the names and images

00:10:11.496 --> 00:10:16.009
of victims of sexual assault or suicide.

00:10:16.033 --> 00:10:19.652
These responsible journalistic practices

00:10:19.676 --> 00:10:22.476
protect public safety

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.883
with zero impact

00:10:24.907 --> 00:10:27.029
on the public's right to know.

00:10:27.717 --> 00:10:30.119
Academic studies show

00:10:31.043 --> 00:10:33.519
that the average news consumer

00:10:33.543 --> 00:10:36.796
wants to hear less about the shooters.

00:10:38.205 --> 00:10:39.416
Instead,

00:10:40.335 --> 00:10:44.315
the media should elevate
the names and images

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:49.397
of the victims,
both murdered and injured,

00:10:49.421 --> 00:10:51.175
the heroes

00:10:51.199 --> 00:10:53.154
and the first responders.

00:10:54.075 --> 00:10:55.227
They should --

00:10:55.251 --> 00:10:58.761
(Applause)

00:11:00.444 --> 00:11:05.076
They should promote data and analysis

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:10.924
from experts on the fields
of mental health and public safety.

00:11:11.643 --> 00:11:13.329
All the experts agree.

00:11:14.189 --> 00:11:16.216
The FBI,

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.000
the International Police Association,

00:11:19.024 --> 00:11:22.680
the Major City Chiefs Association

00:11:22.704 --> 00:11:23.990
and A.L.E.R.T.,

00:11:24.941 --> 00:11:30.646
the law enforcement organization
dedicated to training first responders

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:33.737
to stop active shooters,

00:11:33.761 --> 00:11:37.363
all endorse the principles
of No Notoriety.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.761
In fact, in 2014,

00:11:41.785 --> 00:11:47.275
the FBI started the "Don't Name Them"
campaign in support of the idea.

00:11:47.931 --> 00:11:54.030
The American Psychiatric Association
supports reducing and minimizing

00:11:54.054 --> 00:11:57.329
the identification of these shooters.

00:11:58.258 --> 00:12:01.256
The idea has gone worldwide,

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.047
with the Prime Minister of New Zealand

00:12:04.071 --> 00:12:06.034
calling for no notoriety

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:08.434
after the Christchurch shootings.

00:12:09.595 --> 00:12:14.345
But as much as we want
the media to change,

00:12:14.369 --> 00:12:18.043
they are for-profit organizations.

00:12:18.706 --> 00:12:23.275
They won't change unless
we hold them accountable.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.865
(Applause)

00:12:29.354 --> 00:12:32.889
The media makes their money

00:12:32.913 --> 00:12:34.626
from advertising

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.442
based on the number of viewers and clicks.

00:12:38.983 --> 00:12:45.983
If we can reduce the number
of viewers and clicks on any subject,

00:12:46.007 --> 00:12:49.433
the media will change
the way they report on it.

00:12:50.313 --> 00:12:55.501
So the next time you see
any media organization --

00:12:55.525 --> 00:12:59.818
print, digital, radio or television --

00:12:59.842 --> 00:13:06.320
gratuitously leveraging the names
and images of these shooters,

00:13:06.344 --> 00:13:07.505
stop watching,

00:13:08.406 --> 00:13:10.062
stop listening,

00:13:10.086 --> 00:13:11.930
stop clicking,

00:13:11.954 --> 00:13:13.532
stop liking

00:13:13.556 --> 00:13:15.325
and stop sharing.

00:13:15.349 --> 00:13:19.067
Write to the producers,

00:13:19.091 --> 00:13:23.863
editors, station managers and CEOs

00:13:23.887 --> 00:13:26.123
of these news organizations.

00:13:26.147 --> 00:13:31.292
Take note of the advertisers
who support those segments

00:13:31.316 --> 00:13:33.579
and write to their CEOs.

00:13:34.101 --> 00:13:35.748
Because together,

00:13:36.573 --> 00:13:40.650
we can push the media
to act in the interest

00:13:40.674 --> 00:13:43.010
of public safety,

00:13:43.034 --> 00:13:44.710
not profits.

00:13:46.453 --> 00:13:48.311
It's too late for Alex,

00:13:49.239 --> 00:13:51.422
and it's too late for my family.

00:13:52.108 --> 00:13:55.394
But please don't join
our club by inaction,

00:13:56.315 --> 00:13:58.720
the club nobody wants to join.

00:13:59.378 --> 00:14:01.115
The due's too high.

00:14:02.178 --> 00:14:05.188
Because it's not too late

00:14:05.212 --> 00:14:08.767
for people who aren't victims yet.

00:14:08.791 --> 00:14:10.708
We have the power

00:14:11.795 --> 00:14:16.009
to reduce random mass shootings.

00:14:16.544 --> 00:14:17.827
Let's use it.

00:14:18.264 --> 00:14:19.494
Thank you.

00:14:19.873 --> 00:14:25.119
(Applause)

